    "authorAssociation": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.pick\n\n### Question\n\nHi there, I'm a bit new to this, I want to select files from :Pick git_hunks (To view unstaged files) and when I mark one, this file will be added to stage like (git add filename), I used this feature in telescope, but I don't know how I can do it in Mini.pick. \r\n\r\nSo my question is: Is it possible? mark files and add these to the git stage.",
    "bodyHTML": "<h3 dir=\"auto\">Contributing guidelines</h3>\n<ul class=\"contains-task-list\">\n<li class=\"task-list-item\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"\" disabled=\"\" class=\"task-list-item-checkbox\" aria-label=\"Completed task\" checked=\"\"> I have read <a href=\"https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md\">CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md</a></li>\n</ul>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Module(s)</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">mini.pick</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Question</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Hi there, I'm a bit new to this, I want to select files from :Pick git_hunks (To view unstaged files) and when I mark one, this file will be added to stage like (git add filename), I used this feature in telescope, but I don't know how I can do it in Mini.pick.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">So my question is: Is it possible? mark files and add these to the git stage.</p>",
    "bodyText": "Contributing guidelines\n\n I have read CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md\n\nModule(s)\nmini.pick\nQuestion\nHi there, I'm a bit new to this, I want to select files from :Pick git_hunks (To view unstaged files) and when I mark one, this file will be added to stage like (git add filename), I used this feature in telescope, but I don't know how I can do it in Mini.pick.\nSo my question is: Is it possible? mark files and add these to the git stage.",
    "category": {
        "createdAt": "2022-01-02T14:24:09Z",
        "description": "Ask the community for help",
        "emoji": ":pray:",
        "emojiHTML": "<div>🙏</div>",
        "id": "DIC_kwDOFoksYM4CAgqN",
        "isAnswerable": true,
        "name": "Q&A",
        "slug": "q-a",
        "updatedAt": "2022-01-02T14:24:09Z"
    },
    "closed": true,
    "closedAt": "2025-06-26T09:00:12Z",
    "comment_count": 4,
    "comment_data": [
        {
            "author": {
                "avatarUrl": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/24854248?u=d09fd974c6720eba3039db6beb2f1c1efecdb51d&v=4",
                "login": "echasnovski",
                "resourcePath": "/echasnovski",
                "url": "https://github.com/echasnovski"
            },
            "authorAssociation": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Yes, this (marking hunks, not files, to later apply them) is possible with writing custom `choose_marked`. Something like this:\r\n\r\n```lua\r\nrequire('mini.extra').setup()\r\n\r\nlocal stage_hunk_item = function(item)\r\n  local patch = vim.deepcopy(item.header)\r\n  vim.list_extend(patch, item.hunk)\r\n  local cmd = { 'git', 'apply', '--cached', '-' }\r\n  vim.system(cmd, { stdin = patch }):wait()\r\nend\r\nlocal stage_marked = function(items_marked) vim.tbl_map(stage_hunk_item, items_marked) end\r\n\r\n-- NOTE: Make sure `require('mini.pick').setup()` is called prior to this\r\nMiniPick.registry.git_hunks = function(local_opts)\r\n  MiniExtra.pickers.git_hunks(local_opts, { source = { choose_marked = stage_marked } })\r\nend\r\n```\r\n\r\nSo with this in place:\r\n- `:Pick git_hunks`.\r\n- Mark hunks you'd like to stage (navigate to it and press `<C-x>` with default mappings).\r\n- After all are marked, press `<Alt>+<CR>` with default mappings.\r\n\r\nNote, that this relies on some assumption about the internal structure of items in `git_hunks` picker, but I don't think it will change any time soon.",
            "bodyHTML": "<p dir=\"auto\">Yes, this (marking hunks, not files, to later apply them) is possible with writing custom <code class=\"notranslate\">choose_marked</code>. Something like this:</p>\n<div class=\"highlight highlight-source-lua notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" dir=\"auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"require('mini.extra').setup()\n\nlocal stage_hunk_item = function(item)\n  local patch = vim.deepcopy(item.header)\n  vim.list_extend(patch, item.hunk)\n  local cmd = { 'git', 'apply', '--cached', '-' }\n  vim.system(cmd, { stdin = patch }):wait()\nend\nlocal stage_marked = function(items_marked) vim.tbl_map(stage_hunk_item, items_marked) end\n\n-- NOTE: Make sure `require('mini.pick').setup()` is called prior to this\nMiniPick.registry.git_hunks = function(local_opts)\n  MiniExtra.pickers.git_hunks(local_opts, { source = { choose_marked = stage_marked } })\nend\"><pre class=\"notranslate\"><span class=\"pl-c1\">require</span>(<span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span>mini.extra<span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span></span>).<span class=\"pl-c1\">setup</span>()\n\n<span class=\"pl-k\">local</span> <span class=\"pl-en\">stage_hunk_item</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">function</span>(<span class=\"pl-smi\">item</span>)\n  <span class=\"pl-k\">local</span> <span class=\"pl-smi\">patch</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-smi\">vim</span>.<span class=\"pl-c1\">deepcopy</span>(<span class=\"pl-smi\">item</span>.<span class=\"pl-e\">header</span>)\n  <span class=\"pl-smi\">vim</span>.<span class=\"pl-c1\">list_extend</span>(<span class=\"pl-smi\">patch</span>, <span class=\"pl-smi\">item</span>.<span class=\"pl-e\">hunk</span>)\n  <span class=\"pl-k\">local</span> <span class=\"pl-smi\">cmd</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> { <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span>git<span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span></span>, <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span>apply<span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span></span>, <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span>--cached<span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span></span>, <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span>-<span class=\"pl-pds\">' </span></span>}\n  <span class=\"pl-smi\">vim</span>.<span class=\"pl-c1\">system</span>(<span class=\"pl-smi\">cmd</span>, { <span class=\"pl-smi\">stdin</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-smi\">patch</span> }):<span class=\"pl-c1\">wait</span>()\n<span class=\"pl-k\">end</span>\n<span class=\"pl-k\">local</span> <span class=\"pl-en\">stage_marked</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">function</span>(<span class=\"pl-smi\">items_marked</span>) <span class=\"pl-smi\">vim</span>.<span class=\"pl-c1\">tbl_map</span>(<span class=\"pl-smi\">stage_hunk_item</span>, <span class=\"pl-smi\">items_marked</span>) <span class=\"pl-k\">end</span>\n\n<span class=\"pl-c\"><span class=\"pl-c\">--</span> NOTE: Make sure `require('mini.pick').setup()` is called prior to this</span>\n<span class=\"pl-smi\">MiniPick</span>.<span class=\"pl-e\">registry</span>.<span class=\"pl-en\">git_hunks</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">function</span>(<span class=\"pl-smi\">local_opts</span>)\n  <span class=\"pl-smi\">MiniExtra</span>.<span class=\"pl-e\">pickers</span>.<span class=\"pl-c1\">git_hunks</span>(<span class=\"pl-smi\">local_opts</span>, { <span class=\"pl-smi\">source</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> { <span class=\"pl-smi\">choose_marked</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-smi\">stage_marked</span> } })\n<span class=\"pl-k\">end</span></pre></div>\n<p dir=\"auto\">So with this in place:</p>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li><code class=\"notranslate\">:Pick git_hunks</code>.</li>\n<li>Mark hunks you'd like to stage (navigate to it and press <code class=\"notranslate\">&lt;C-x&gt;</code> with default mappings).</li>\n<li>After all are marked, press <code class=\"notranslate\">&lt;Alt&gt;+&lt;CR&gt;</code> with default mappings.</li>\n</ul>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Note, that this relies on some assumption about the internal structure of items in <code class=\"notranslate\">git_hunks</code> picker, but I don't think it will change any time soon.</p>",
            "bodyText": "Yes, this (marking hunks, not files, to later apply them) is possible with writing custom choose_marked. Something like this:\nrequire('mini.extra').setup()\n\nlocal stage_hunk_item = function(item)\n  local patch = vim.deepcopy(item.header)\n  vim.list_extend(patch, item.hunk)\n  local cmd = { 'git', 'apply', '--cached', '-' }\n  vim.system(cmd, { stdin = patch }):wait()\nend\nlocal stage_marked = function(items_marked) vim.tbl_map(stage_hunk_item, items_marked) end\n\n-- NOTE: Make sure `require('mini.pick').setup()` is called prior to this\nMiniPick.registry.git_hunks = function(local_opts)\n  MiniExtra.pickers.git_hunks(local_opts, { source = { choose_marked = stage_marked } })\nend\nSo with this in place:\n\n:Pick git_hunks.\nMark hunks you'd like to stage (navigate to it and press <C-x> with default mappings).\nAfter all are marked, press <Alt>+<CR> with default mappings.\n\nNote, that this relies on some assumption about the internal structure of items in git_hunks picker, but I don't think it will change any time soon.",
