                    "authorAssociation": "MEMBER",
                    "body": "What colors do you want to change and where? If it about preview, then try adjusting highlight groups like `diff***`. To see available highlight groups, you can do `:h diff` and press `<Tab>`. The ones that start with \"diff\" (and *not* \"Diff\") are used for 'diff' files.\r\n\r\nI right now realized that `:Pick git_hunks` preview doesn't try to use tree-sitter, but it should. After it is added, if there is tree-sitter parser installed for 'diff' language, then it will be more complicated. It will be highlight groups with `.diff` suffix. Like `@diff.added.diff`, `@function.diff`, etc. One way to see specific groups, is to use 'mini.git' and run `:Git diff`. It should show diff with tree-sitter enabled (if set up properly) and then using `:Inspect` will show highlight groups under cursor.",
                    "bodyHTML": "<p dir=\"auto\">What colors do you want to change and where? If it about preview, then try adjusting highlight groups like <code class=\"notranslate\">diff***</code>. To see available highlight groups, you can do <code class=\"notranslate\">:h diff</code> and press <code class=\"notranslate\">&lt;Tab&gt;</code>. The ones that start with \"diff\" (and <em>not</em> \"Diff\") are used for 'diff' files.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">I right now realized that <code class=\"notranslate\">:Pick git_hunks</code> preview doesn't try to use tree-sitter, but it should. After it is added, if there is tree-sitter parser installed for 'diff' language, then it will be more complicated. It will be highlight groups with <code class=\"notranslate\">.diff</code> suffix. Like <code class=\"notranslate\">@diff.added.diff</code>, <code class=\"notranslate\">@function.diff</code>, etc. One way to see specific groups, is to use 'mini.git' and run <code class=\"notranslate\">:Git diff</code>. It should show diff with tree-sitter enabled (if set up properly) and then using <code class=\"notranslate\">:Inspect</code> will show highlight groups under cursor.</p>",
                    "bodyText": "What colors do you want to change and where? If it about preview, then try adjusting highlight groups like diff***. To see available highlight groups, you can do :h diff and press <Tab>. The ones that start with \"diff\" (and not \"Diff\") are used for 'diff' files.\nI right now realized that :Pick git_hunks preview doesn't try to use tree-sitter, but it should. After it is added, if there is tree-sitter parser installed for 'diff' language, then it will be more complicated. It will be highlight groups with .diff suffix. Like @diff.added.diff, @function.diff, etc. One way to see specific groups, is to use 'mini.git' and run :Git diff. It should show diff with tree-sitter enabled (if set up properly) and then using :Inspect will show highlight groups under cursor.",
