                {
                    "author": {
                        "avatarUrl": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/24854248?u=d09fd974c6720eba3039db6beb2f1c1efecdb51d&v=4",
                        "login": "echasnovski",
                        "resourcePath": "/echasnovski",
                        "url": "https://github.com/echasnovski"
                    },
                    "authorAssociation": "MEMBER",
                    "body": "> @echasnovski any chance this action can go to mini.extra for the hunks picker? This can be made the official way to stage and unstage multiple hunks.\r\n\r\nAt the moment, I don't think so. The main idea behind pickers that reference file/buffer positions/regions is that their default usage should navigate to that position/region. The \"choose marked\" action is similar by placing all of them into quickfix list and allowing to navigate through them.\r\n\r\nIt *might* be considered a separate action, but I don't really think it is a good idea. There is 'mini.diff' for applying hunks (and can be used together with quickfix list approach to stage hunks, but not unstage sadly) and more comprehensive Git tools designed to integrate with it (I use and recommend Lazygit).",
                    "bodyHTML": "<blockquote>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><a class=\"user-mention notranslate\" data-hovercard-type=\"user\" data-hovercard-url=\"/users/echasnovski/hovercard\" data-octo-click=\"hovercard-link-click\" data-octo-dimensions=\"link_type:self\" href=\"https://github.com/echasnovski\">@echasnovski</a> any chance this action can go to mini.extra for the hunks picker? This can be made the official way to stage and unstage multiple hunks.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p dir=\"auto\">At the moment, I don't think so. The main idea behind pickers that reference file/buffer positions/regions is that their default usage should navigate to that position/region. The \"choose marked\" action is similar by placing all of them into quickfix list and allowing to navigate through them.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">It <em>might</em> be considered a separate action, but I don't really think it is a good idea. There is 'mini.diff' for applying hunks (and can be used together with quickfix list approach to stage hunks, but not unstage sadly) and more comprehensive Git tools designed to integrate with it (I use and recommend Lazygit).</p>",
                    "bodyText": "@echasnovski any chance this action can go to mini.extra for the hunks picker? This can be made the official way to stage and unstage multiple hunks.\n\nAt the moment, I don't think so. The main idea behind pickers that reference file/buffer positions/regions is that their default usage should navigate to that position/region. The \"choose marked\" action is similar by placing all of them into quickfix list and allowing to navigate through them.\nIt might be considered a separate action, but I don't really think it is a good idea. There is 'mini.diff' for applying hunks (and can be used together with quickfix list approach to stage hunks, but not unstage sadly) and more comprehensive Git tools designed to integrate with it (I use and recommend Lazygit).",
